e prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record for Sutton County runs 75 years, from 1951 to 2025, on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids. January to February and March to April each came in under 90% of normal in 39 of those years. In 2025, June to July hit 249% of normal on the middle of the grids, while February to March sat at 35%. Every grid had its driest year in 1951, with grids 12718 and 12719 down at 35%.</p>"}
